<title>UK: Mexico adds $250 mln to 20-year bond at +445 bp.</title>
<headline>Mexico adds $250 mln to 20-year bond at +445 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond announced yesterday has been increased by $250 million.</p>
<p>The pricing has also been changed to 445 b.p. over U.S. Treasuries from the previous indicated range of 450-462.5 b.p., joint lead managers Goldman Sachs International and Merrill Lynch International said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   MEXICO</p>
<p> AMT   *$1.0 BLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    15.SEP.16</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE 25/26.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  =	   REOFFER    **	  SPREAD***+445 BP</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.0 PCT FEB 2026 U.S. TREASURY BOND</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED</p>
<p>		SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>	     *ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR $750 MILLION.</p>
<p>	   ***PREVIOUS INDICATED SPREAD 450-462.5 B.P.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
